WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
The task is finished.

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:02.940
The confirmation arrived.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:04.680
But did it help?

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.200
Before we talk about artificial
intelligence, consider an ordinary

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.600
decision: arranging an outing
for a group of people.

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.893
A volunteer reserves a room
for a weekend group outing.

00:00:17.693 --> 00:00:18.553
The booking is confirmed.

00:00:19.313 --> 00:00:22.413
But the time conflicts with the
last bus home for two members.

00:00:22.973 --> 00:00:25.113
They say they cannot attend at that time.

00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:29.065
The volunteer can ask about another slot.

00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:32.485
Only the group coordinator can
commit to changing the booking.

00:00:33.345 --> 00:00:37.585
The coordinator says: The reservation
succeeded, so the outing is arranged.

00:00:38.917 --> 00:00:41.217
What should happen next, and why?

00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:45.357
Pause the video and write your decision
before hearing the discussion.

00:00:46.237 --> 00:00:49.657
You can leave the final choice open
if you explain what you still need

00:00:49.657 --> 00:00:50.017
to know.

00:00:50.528 --> 00:00:59.542
[Pause and write your answer.
Take the time you need.]

00:00:59.542 --> 00:01:02.382
Would a small table help
you explain this situation?

00:01:02.382 --> 00:01:06.182
Or would a written account preserve
something the table loses?

00:01:07.302 --> 00:01:07.962
Either can work.

00:01:08.922 --> 00:01:12.282
Keep the affected people and
the unresolved facts in view.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.830
Here is one way to separate the facts.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.070
What happened: a room reservation was confirmed.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:25.610
What people need: an outing the
intended participants can actually

00:01:25.610 --> 00:01:25.910
attend.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:29.910
What remains open: two members
report a travel conflict.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:32.270
Other times and costs are unknown.

00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:37.425
The booking record supports a narrow
claim: there is a reservation.

00:01:38.245 --> 00:01:40.345
It does not establish that everyone can attend.

00:01:41.165 --> 00:01:45.085
A defensible next step is to ask about
alternatives and hear the affected

00:01:45.085 --> 00:01:48.125
members before promising that
the outing is fully arranged.

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.767
Now another organizer objects.

00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:54.727
People have already planned around this time.

00:01:55.387 --> 00:01:58.747
Moving the outing could inconvenience
them, or exclude someone else.

00:01:59.547 --> 00:02:00.467
That objection matters.

00:02:01.207 --> 00:02:04.687
Asking about alternatives does not
yet justify changing the booking.

00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:11.443
Compare a different time, travel support
if it is feasible, postponement,

00:02:11.983 --> 00:02:15.743
and keeping the booking with the
exclusion explicitly acknowledged.

00:02:16.863 --> 00:02:18.923
Hear from the people who bear each cost.

00:02:19.863 --> 00:02:21.823
The coordinator has a decision role.

00:02:22.543 --> 00:02:24.763
That role does not make every choice fair.

00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:27.665
What would change your judgment?

00:02:28.745 --> 00:02:31.745
Name a specific fact that
could change your next step.

00:02:32.705 --> 00:02:34.185
Pause and write it down.

00:02:34.816 --> 00:02:42.833
[Pause and write your answer.
Take the time you need.]

00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:47.133
Perhaps the two members identify
an acceptable travel option.

00:02:47.873 --> 00:02:50.873
Perhaps a different time
would exclude more people.

00:02:51.933 --> 00:02:53.573
Neither is established in this story.

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:55.973
Either could change the next step.

00:02:56.733 --> 00:03:01.153
Neither would make the original confirmation
proof that the whole arrangement

00:03:01.153 --> 00:03:01.593
worked.

00:03:03.042 --> 00:03:06.322
A conversation and a list of
alternatives may be enough.

00:03:07.122 --> 00:03:10.822
Changing a booking does not necessarily
recover preparation time or

00:03:10.822 --> 00:03:11.682
missed participation.

00:03:12.662 --> 00:03:16.762
This is the consequences lens we
are starting with in SideFX: when

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:21.362
someone says a task is complete,
ask which result they mean, and who

00:03:21.362 --> 00:03:23.062
still cannot get what they need.

00:03:24.417 --> 00:03:27.177
Think of one completed task in your own work.

00:03:27.897 --> 00:03:29.537
Whose result might still be unresolved?

00:03:30.697 --> 00:03:33.457
Describe the missing result and
the evidence you would need.

00:03:34.297 --> 00:03:37.097
Next, we will ask: What do we actually know?
